  "description": "An attention identifier none of the four handled keys names: the WHEN OTHER arm at :132-136. COUSR00C tests EIBAID inline - it is one of the twelve programs that do not COPY CSSTRPFY - and the migration routes those tests through the single common.PfKeyResolver, which must reproduce them as identical boolean outcomes: PF9 resolves to a key that is none of ENTER, PF3, PF7 or PF8, so it joins WHEN OTHER exactly as the inline tests put it there. The arm raises the error flag, moves -1 into USRIDINL to place the cursor, and paints CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY from app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy - a 50-character literal whose trailing spaces are significant, moved into the 80-byte WS-MESSAGE and then narrowed to the 78-byte ERRMSGO. No browse is opened.",
